<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Gambhir Singh</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1788">1788</a>–<a href="/years/1834">1834</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/19th-century">19th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Gambhir Singh was a prince of the Manipuri royal house who led the Manipur Levy, raised with British help, to drive the Burmese out of Manipur during the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/first-anglo-burmese-war">First Anglo-Burmese War</a>. He was restored as raja in 1826 under the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/treaty-of-yandabo">Treaty of Yandabo</a> and recovered the Kabaw valley region for a time.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/gambhir-singh.jpg" alt="Gambhir Singh" width="320" height="430" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Moirangthemcha · CC BY-SA 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Gambhirsingh.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
